WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.541
[MUSIC]

00:00:07.541 --> 00:00:11.684
How do you decide then whether or not you
have a shot at getting into Stanford?

00:00:11.684 --> 00:00:14.582
&gt;&gt; That's a great question, that's
probably the million-dollar question.

00:00:14.582 --> 00:00:18.742
And I'm hoping all of what we discuss
today will give applicants insight into

00:00:18.742 --> 00:00:20.780
whether or not they have a shot.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.910
But, I think if I had
to go to the essence,

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:26.900
what is absolutely most important
in making that decision,

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:30.530
we're trying to answer two questions
on the admissions committee.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.319
The first is,
is this particular applicant going to be

00:00:33.319 --> 00:00:36.060
engaged academically when
they come to our program?

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:40.950
And the second is, what kind of impact
will they have after they graduate?

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:45.583
And if you think, well, we care about
their educational engagement because we're

00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:49.517
a higher education institution,
we want our classroom to be vibrant.

00:00:49.517 --> 00:00:53.400
You probably know as a student the more
interested folks are when they're learning

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.187
and curious the better and
richer that experience will be.

00:00:56.187 --> 00:00:59.950
And then on the flip side,
we do care and believe in our tag line.

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:03.300
We want to know when we're
selecting these students that they

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.890
have the potential to change lives, change
organizations, and change the world.

